Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||04-09-99||10:09 PM||||I saw a post on a newsgroup regarding the possibility of putting a power steering unit into a Fiero. Anyone here know if that's possible, and if so, where a compatible unit might be found? (another GM car maybe?)<br>Power steering is something I definitely want in a kit.. so I'd really be interested in hearing about this. thanks.
Z||000001||Punkndrublic||04-10-99||02:29 AM||||They made an electric power steering pump that was available from pontiac. but i think only the 88's had the mounting holes to put it in though.
Z||000002||theogre||04-10-99||08:55 PM||||there probably are power racks from other GM cars that would fit. The Fiero's problem was engine compartment space more than anything. there's no place to put a pump for traditional hydraulic systems.<p>that I know of GM never put the electric system into production for any of its cars.<br>
